## Overview

`TxMotionLoader` preserves the 134 named Amicro loading implementations and the three additional CSS loaders. Each variant has its own source geometry, trajectory, phase offsets and cadence. The catalog below keeps the original IDs and exported names. This is an indeterminate loading indicator; it never reports business completion.

The root is a polite status region with a stable accessible label. Animated artwork is hidden from assistive technology. Playback requires `playing=true`, a mounted visible component, a visible document and no reduced-motion preference. When any gate closes, native animations are cancelled and readable static artwork remains. Resuming starts the source rhythm again.

## Usage

### All named scenes

Filter the complete catalog, control each scene or all scenes, and adjust size, speed and localized status text. All 137 entries are mounted in the scrollable catalog; entries outside the viewport do not animate.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="MotionLoaderDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxMotionLoader
      variant="anim-apple-spinner"
      :playing="true"
      size="sm"
      :speed="1.5"
      :labels="{ loading: 'Loading', paused: 'Paused' }"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Controlled playback

`playing` requests playback; visibility and reduced-motion settings still take priority. Change the source ID to switch geometry. The previous scene is disposed before the next scene starts.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref } from 'vue'
import { TxMotionLoader } from '@talex-touch/tuffex'

const playing = ref(true)
</script>

<template>
  <TxMotionLoader variant="wave-physics-loader" :playing="playing" />
  <button type="button" @click="playing = !playing">Toggle playback</button>
</template>
```

### Best Practices

- Prefer `TxSkeleton` or `TxRowSkeleton` for first-load content placeholders. Choose a motion loader for a short indeterminate wait whose geometry suits the surface.
- Keep `playing` tied to actual pending work. Pausing an animation does not mean the request has completed, so the status region remains busy.
- Supply `label` and `labels` for the host locale. The text variants use those labels, including per-character wave and pop scenes.
- Use `TxProgressBar` when progress is known. No loader simulates percentages or succeeds after a timer.
- Keep speed moderate and let the component own offscreen, hidden-page, KeepAlive and reduced-motion suspension.

## API Reference

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `variant` | `MotionLoaderVariant` | `'classic-spinner'` | Exact source ID from the 137-entry catalog below. |
| `playing` | `boolean` | `true` | Requests playback. False cancels all native tracks and leaves readable static artwork. |
| `size` | `'xs' \| 'sm' \| 'md' \| 'lg'` | `'md'` | Source-geometry scale: 0.65, 0.85, 1 and 1.25. Aspect ratios and phase distances stay source-defined. |
| `speed` | `number` | `1` | Positive playback-rate multiplier. Non-finite or non-positive values use 1. |
| `label` | `string` | `labels.loading` | Accessible status name and visible status copy; independent of the artwork's words. |
| `labels` | `MotionLoaderLabels` | See below | Localized words for textual scenes and paused status. |
| `showLabel` | `boolean` | `true` | Shows status text. False visually clips it without removing it from the accessibility tree. |

#### Labels

| Key | Default | Used by |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `loading` | `'Loading'` | Status copy, AppleTextReveal, Typing, TextMorph and SpringTextPop. SpringTextPop appends the source's three dots. |
| `thinking` | `'Thinking'` | TextBlink, TextDots, TextShimmer and TextShimmerWave. |
| `waiting` | `'Wait'` | The second TextMorph layer. |
| `unlock` | `'Slide to unlock'` | Both AppleUnlock shimmer layers. |
| `terminal` | `'loading...'` | TerminalLoader's command text; cursor and prompt keep their source geometry. |
| `paused` | `'Paused'` | Status text when `playing=false`. |

### Events

No component-specific events. The host controls pending work and the `playing` prop.

### Slots

No slots. Textual scene content comes from `labels`; generic artwork is not substituted for missing content.

### Exports

- `TxMotionLoader` and the installed `MotionLoader` component.
- `MOTION_LOADER_VARIANTS`: readonly tuple enumerating all 137 source IDs; `MotionLoaderVariant` is derived from that tuple.
- `MOTION_LOADER_SOURCES`: typed records containing each `id`, original exported `name` and pinned upstream `source` path.
- `MotionLoaderProps`, `MotionLoaderLabels`, `MotionLoaderSize`, `MotionLoaderSource` and `TxMotionLoaderInstance`.

