## Technologies

Source declarations render native HTML/SVG without React, Framer Motion or Tailwind runtime. Web Animations preserves separate property tracks, explicit keyframe stops and staggered delays. Spring-marked scenes use the shared TuffEx `resolveTransition` compiler. Text changes use `TxTextMorph`; Skeleton, SkeletonLoader and FluidSkeleton compose the existing `TxSkeleton` geometry without a second unmanaged skeleton loop.

WavePhysicsLoader retains 15 bars, 201 sampled phases, four parabolic bounces per crossing, the cosine influence radius, impact indentation and ball squash/stretch. Its four-second round trip is not replaced by a generic wave. The 292px source scene has a 0.38 native presentation scale before the public size multiplier.

TextDots retains its three source stop lists: `[0, 0.2, 0.8, 1]`, `[0, 0.4, 0.8, 1]` and `[0, 0.6, 0.8, 1]`. MatrixGridLoader retains `[0, 0.5, 0.75, 1]` with the four delays 0.2, 0.4, 0.8 and 0.6 seconds. AppleEqualizer freezes the source's random delay samples to 0.06, 0.41, 0.19 and 0.32 seconds for deterministic SSR rather than generating a new random rhythm during hydration. Colors use theme tokens; SVG goo filter IDs use Vue's hydration-stable `useId()`.

The shared `useMotionActivity` owns visibility, reduced-motion and KeepAlive lifecycle gates. Each scene owns and cancels its native animations on suspension, source replacement and unmount. Browsers without Web Animations retain the same static artwork.
